(vas: assemble the NASM-dialect source the Vox compiler writes into a
 static x86-64 executable. The work is the vas library's; this program
 reads the command line, makes one call, and passes the diagnostics on to
 standard error.)

see "./vas.vox".

A flag called 'wants help' is "--help" or "-h", it is a boolean.
A flag called 'output path' is "--output" or "-o", it is a text.
A flag called 'coreasm directory given' is "--coreasm" or "-c", it is a text.
Parse flags.

A text called program is arguments's name.

If 'wants help' then,
    Print "Usage: {program} [OPTION]... SOURCE -o OUTPUT",
    Print "Assemble SOURCE, the assembly the Vox compiler writes, into the static",
    Print "x86-64 executable OUTPUT, the way nasm and ld would build it.",
    Print "\nOptions:",
    Print "  -o, --output FILE   write the executable to FILE; there is no default",
    Print "  -c, --coreasm DIR   look for the compiler's coreasm in DIR, for the",
    Print "                      source's %include lines (default: the directory",
    Print "                      VOX_CORE_PATH names, else /usr/share/vox/coreasm)",
    Print "  -h, --help          display this help and exit",
    Print "\nThe executable is written with mode 0644, so make it executable with chmod.",
    Print "Nothing is written when the source has errors. The exit status is the",
    Print "number of errors, or 255 when there are more than 255, and each error is",
    Print "one line on standard error.",
    Exit 0.

Open a file for writing called 'error stream' at 2 (standard error).

a list called 'source paths' is arguments's all.
If 'source paths''s length is not 1 then,
    Write "{program}: name exactly one source; try --help\n" to 'error stream',
    Exit 2.
If 'output path' is empty then,
    Write "{program}: name the output with -o; try --help\n" to 'error stream',
    Exit 2.

a text called 'coreasm directory' is 'coreasm directory given'.
If 'coreasm directory' is empty then,
    If the environment variable "VOX_CORE_PATH" exists then,
        Set 'coreasm directory' to environment's "VOX_CORE_PATH"..
If 'coreasm directory' is empty then,
    Set 'coreasm directory' to "/usr/share/vox/coreasm".

a text called 'source path' is element 1 of 'source paths'.
a text called messages is 'assemble the file' of 'source path' and 'coreasm directory' and 'output path'.
Write messages to 'error stream'.

(Each diagnostic is one line, so the newlines count the errors. An exit
 status is one byte, so a count it cannot hold is given as its largest
 value, as the help says.)
a buffer called diagnostics is "{messages}".
a number called 'error count' is 0.
For each character from diagnostics, if character is '\n' then, increment 'error count'..
If 'error count' is greater than 255 then, Set 'error count' to 255.
Exit 'error count'.
